From: Bkacjios
Subject: [PATCH] PocketGo S30: armv7 musl (Alpine), clang, ARMv7 libm, portrait panel

Runs GameMaker Android titles (AM2R) on the PocketGo S30: Allwinner A33
(Cortex-A7, ARMv7), Alpine (musl), GLES 2 on a portrait panel.

- musl: the glibc extensions it lacks (s30/musl_compat.h, s30/musl_extra.cpp);
  generate_libc.py parses the target sysroot (GML_CLANG_EXTRA), skips cursor
  kinds older bindings lack, and only calls a function ambiguous when two
  declarations differ
- bionic armv7 has a 32-bit time_t/off_t/rlim_t/sigset_t, musl 64-bit (128-byte
  sigset): converting wrappers (thunks/libc/bionic32.cpp) for time, stat,
  offsets, mmap, rlimits, signals and sigsetjmp; BIONIC_FILE is 84 bytes
  (BIONIC_fpos_t a long); the stdio wrappers unwrap the FILE bridge
- clang: the JNI table has the guest ABI (pcs("aapcs")); bionic div_t etc.
  alias the host types
- the shipped AOSP libm.so is ARMv8-A code: the host libm instead
  (thunks/libm/libm.cpp)
- a portrait window: the game draws landscape offscreen, shown rotated
  (gmloader/s30_rotate.cpp)
- first_pad_slot (config): AM2R reads gamepad slot 1
- crash report with guest module offsets; S30_GML_INPUT_LOG=1 logs input

